/**
 * Count distinct, paid incoming orders in an accepted tenant-scoped snapshot.
 *
 * context: {session: {user: {id, tenant_id, role}}, tenantId?}. Passing the
 * session directly ({user: ...}) is also supported. An explicit null session
 * means logged out, even when an old snapshot still contains its former user.
 * Without a context, the authenticated state.user projection is used; Flask's
 * existing projection has id/role but deliberately omits tenant_id.
 *
 * This is the provisional outstanding-work count, not unread notifications or
 * today's column count. It includes earlier/future pickup dates in the snapshot
 * so a date rollover cannot silently clear unfinished work. It does not decide
 * whether a refund REQUEST alone should hold a handoff; that policy is separate.
 * Freshness/auth epoch/revision validation belongs to the sync caller. Call this
 * function again on each accepted snapshot; never increment its result by event.
 * This selector is not a replacement for server authorization.
